{%- comment -%}
  Ceremonial loader — signature brand moment.

  Loader intentionally disabled pending approved walking Oryx animation and final House Seal
  asset verification — see config/settings_data.json (enable_loader: false) and the header comment
  in assets/caviera-loader.js. The markup, settings and cascade logic below are untouched and
  remain fully ready; re-enable by flipping enable_loader back to true once real assets are
  approved. (This comment is internal-only — it never reaches the public storefront.)

  This is the ONLY loader implementation in the theme (no sections/caviera-loader.liquid exists —
  do not recreate one). Rendered unconditionally via `{% render 'caviera-loader' %}` inside
  `{% if template.name == 'index' %}` in layout/theme.liquid.

  Controlled-visual-test revision: base field is now Obsidian by default (was Cinnabar) — "OBSIDIAN
  full-screen field → Oryx → House Seal → Master Signature → reveal". The exit is no longer a plain
  opacity fade: assets/caviera-loader.css's `.is-leaving` sweeps the whole field away on a transform
  (translateY), so the field itself reads as "a controlled curtain moving away", per brief. Default
  total ceremony budget (data-duration 2200ms + the ~700ms sweep) targets the ~2–3s maximum.

  IMPORTANT — two independent layers of "always present":
    1. The root `[data-caviera-loader]` always renders on the homepage, regardless of
       settings.enable_loader, session state, or asset availability.
    2. All three child stage wrappers — `[data-loader-oryx]`, `[data-loader-seal]`, and
       `[data-loader-signature]` — ALSO always render inside the root, regardless of asset
       availability. Only the actual `<img>` *inside* each wrapper is conditional. This keeps "does
       the markup exist" (Liquid's job) fully separate from "does it visibly run"
       (assets/caviera-loader.css hides it by default; assets/caviera-loader.js decides at runtime
       whether to activate, and which stage(s) have real artwork to show). Each stage selector
       therefore always resolves on the homepage, even when a wrapper's image is empty.

  Asset cascade (see docs/required-brand-assets.md for the full policy). The Master Signature stage
  (Phase 1 addition) only ever plays as the closing beat of a sequence that already has something
  to resolve from — it never appears alone with neither oryx nor seal configured:
    1. Oryx + House Seal + Master Signature → oryx walk → crossfade to seal → crossfade to the
       Master Signature → fade into the hero.
    2. Oryx + House Seal, no Master Signature → oryx walk → crossfade to seal → fade into the hero
       (unchanged from before this stage existed).
    3. Oryx only, no seal        → walk stage only, then fades straight into the hero.
    4. House Seal only, no oryx → the seal alone, held briefly and static — never an unofficial
       substitute mascot. Master Signature may still follow if configured.
    5. Neither Oryx nor Seal approved → all wrappers exist (empty) for inspection/dev tooling; the
       loader stays inert on the public storefront. A Theme-Editor-only note (request.design_mode)
       names the exact missing setting(s) — never shown to real visitors.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign has_oryx = false
  if settings.oryx_full or settings.oryx_walk
    assign has_oryx = true
  endif

  assign seal_mode = blank
  if settings.seal_on_dark
    assign seal_mode = 'dark'
  elsif settings.seal_on_light
    assign seal_mode = 'light'
  endif
  assign has_seal = false
  unless seal_mode == blank
    assign has_seal = true
  endunless

  assign has_signature = false
  if settings.master_signature_on_dark or settings.master_signature_on_light
    assign has_signature = true
  endif
-%}
<div
  class="caviera-loader"
  data-caviera-loader
  data-enabled="{{ settings.enable_loader }}"
  data-once-per-session="{{ settings.loader_once_per_session }}"
  data-duration="{{ settings.loader_duration | default: 2200 }}"
  data-reduced-motion-behaviour="{{ settings.loader_reduced_motion | default: 'static_brief' }}"
  data-design-mode="{{ request.design_mode }}"
  data-has-oryx="{{ has_oryx }}"
  data-has-seal="{{ has_seal }}"
  data-has-signature="{{ has_signature }}"
  style="--loader-bg: {{ settings.loader_background | default: '#111012' }};"
  aria-hidden="true"
>
  <div class="caviera-loader__stage caviera-loader__oryx" data-loader-oryx>
    {%- if has_oryx -%}
      {%- render 'caviera-oryx', variant: 'walk', width: 220, loading: 'eager', fetchpriority: 'high' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <div class="caviera-loader__stage caviera-loader__seal" data-loader-seal>
    {%- if has_seal -%}
      {%- render 'caviera-house-seal', mode: seal_mode, width: 72, loading: 'eager', fetchpriority: 'high' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <div class="caviera-loader__stage caviera-loader__signature" data-loader-signature>
    {%- if has_signature -%}
      {%- render 'caviera-master-signature', mode: 'dark', width: 220, loading: 'eager', fetchpriority: 'high' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- if request.design_mode and has_oryx == false and has_seal == false and has_signature == false -%}
    <p class="caviera-loader__editor-note">
      Ceremonial loader is wired but has nothing to show yet — upload a Full-body oryx, House Seal,
      or Master Signature under Theme settings → CAVIERA Identity. (Visible only here, inside the
      Theme Editor.)
    </p>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
<script src="{{ 'caviera-loader.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
